BT /F2 16 Tf 72 710 Td (Chapter 1 – The Cloud Shaped Like a Bed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 680 Td (Bo the bear was almost asleep when something caught his eye.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 662 Td (Outside his window floated a cloud — soft and wide —) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 644 Td (shaped exactly like his favourite bed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 626 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 608 Td ("Hello," Bo said.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 590 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 572 Td (The cloud drifted closer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 554 Td ("Would you like a ride?" it seemed to say.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 536 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 518 Td (Bo stepped onto it. It was even softer than it looked.) Tj ET
endstream
