BT /F2 16 Tf 72 710 Td (Chapter 4 – The Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 680 Td (Bo looked at all his dream bubbles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 662 Td (He chose the brightest one — the dream of laughing —) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 644 Td (and tucked it carefully under his arm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 626 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 608 Td (When the cloud brought him home, Bo slipped quietly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 590 Td (into his little sister's room and left the bubble on her pillow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 572 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 554 Td (He never told her where it came from.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 536 Td (But the next morning, she woke up smiling.) Tj ET
